# ============================================================
# INTERNAL DOCUMENTS — KEEP OUT OF SEARCH RESULTS
# ============================================================
# These are working documents, not marketing pages. They stay reachable
# at their normal addresses so you can open them, but they must never
# appear in a search result.
#
# X-Robots-Tag is the mechanism that matters: it is a response header,
# so it is only read after a crawler has actually fetched the page.
# A robots.txt "Disallow" cannot do this job, because a blocked
# crawler never downloads the page and so never sees the instruction.
# Both are set below so the documents are doubly excluded.
#
# The wildcard covers both forms of every address — /docs and
# /docs.html — because Cloudflare serves the extensionless form.
#
# NOTE: this is not access control. Anyone who already knows a URL
# can still open the page. It keeps search engines out; it does not
# keep people out.
/docs*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
/app-documentation*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
/pricing-benchmark-report*
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex, nofollow, noarchive
/brand-guidelines*
